<h5>Posts</h5>
<p>Write blog posts with excerpt, category, featured image, optional <strong>visual layout builder</strong> (frontend editor — modules include heading, text, image, <strong>carousel</strong>, <strong>accordion</strong>, <strong>tabs</strong>, <strong>icon list</strong>, <strong>gallery</strong>, <strong>testimonials</strong>, <strong>video</strong>, <strong>inner row</strong>, button, CTA, blurb, and more) and optional <strong>block builder</strong>, tags (comma-separated), publish date, and optional <strong>content width</strong> override for the public post layout. Visual layout takes precedence over blocks and body when saved. When a visual layout is saved, the public post does <strong>not</strong> repeat the title or featured image above the layout (those stay for the blog list, SEO, and social sharing). In the frontend editor: use <strong>Desktop / Tablet / Mobile</strong> preview (and the same buttons to edit tablet/mobile Design), <strong>Templates</strong> to reuse layouts, <strong>Layers</strong> (with a filter; drag to reorder) for the structure tree, choose column layouts per row, add modules from the described side-panel picker (or <strong>+</strong> after a module), add <strong>Inner row</strong> to split a column again (one nested row only), edit Content / Design / Advanced (Content shows the fields for that module type, including carousel slides, accordion/tabs/icon-list items, gallery photos, testimonials, and a Video URL — YouTube, Vimeo, or HTTPS file only; Text, CTA, and Blurb bodies plus Accordion/Tabs item bodies use a Bold / Italic / list / Link toolbar — scripts and extra tags are stripped on save; headings stay plain; Custom HTML is still for embeds; Design fields depend on the module (Heading includes type, Spacer is spacing only); Design colors can use theme tokens; sections can set a background image and overlay, allowlisted shape dividers, and a video background (canvas never plays the embed); row Content can reverse columns on mobile; module Design has Normal / Hover when the module has color, type, or chrome, allowlisted Font / Letter spacing / Text transform, border/corners/shadow, and Copy style / Paste style; Advanced has sticky position and z-index (1–100); Content edits update the selected module without a full canvas rebuild), type heading/text on the canvas, <strong>Copy</strong> / <strong>Paste</strong> (Ctrl/Cmd+C / V or right-click), press <strong>?</strong> for shortcuts, drag <strong>⋮⋮</strong> to reorder, and set column <strong>width (1–12)</strong> and <strong>min height</strong> (or drag the column edge). Text align on Design applies to inner wrappers too (Blurb stays centered until you set it). Design colors, spacing, and min height apply live without rebuilding the canvas. Inspector crumbs jump to a parent section/row/column. <strong>Undo / Redo</strong> (Ctrl/Cmd+Z / Y), Ctrl/Cmd+S save, Ctrl/Cmd+D duplicate; dirty layouts autosave about every 12 seconds. Button and CTA modules can open links in a new tab. <strong>Revisions</strong> appear on the post view screen for rollback. Published posts appear on <code>/blog</code> (listing layout — list/grid/cards/magazine/compact, columns, and visitor view switcher — under Appearance → Customize or System → General → Public site theme).</p>
<p><strong>Create everything on the form:</strong> Upload featured or block images here; click tag chips or type new tag names (auto-created); add a new category without leaving the editor.</p>
<p><strong>Duplicate:</strong> List and view screens have <strong>Duplicate</strong> (creates a draft copy including layout, tags, SEO, and password protection; not pinned). Needs <code>add_posts</code>.</p>
<p><strong>Bulk actions:</strong> On the posts list, select rows and Apply: Publish, Set to draft, Pin to top, Unpin, or Delete (max 100). Publish/pin need <code>edit_posts</code>; delete needs <code>delete_posts</code>.</p>
<p><strong>List sort &amp; filters:</strong> Click a column header to sort (toggle direction; date columns start newest first). <strong>Created</strong> is available alongside <strong>Published</strong>. Filter by status (including scheduled), category, author, pinned, and a published or created date range.</p>
<p><strong>Password protect:</strong> Same as pages — optional visitor password on the post form. Blog lists still show the title (excerpt is hidden until unlocked). RSS includes the title with a stub description. Comments stay off until the post is unlocked. Logged-in editors with <code>edit_posts</code> skip the gate. Playwright: <code>npm run test:e2e:cms-pulse-ux</code>.</p>
<p><strong>Import:</strong> <code>/admin/posts/import</code> (or <code>php cli/import_atom_feed.php path/to/feed.atom</code>) accepts an Atom / Blogger export. Start from <code>docs/samples/cms-atom-import/sample.atom</code> (backdated, scheduled, draft, PAGE, and optional native SEO/AEO fields). Enriched feeds may declare the documented <code>cms</code> namespace and provide SEO title, LLM summary, citation snippet, FAQ JSON, and noindex. Supplied <code>cms:*</code> values overwrite on update; omitted values preserve existing metadata. Feed publish times become <strong>Publish at</strong>: a past datetime is live; a future datetime stays off the public site, RSS, and sitemap until that clock time (no cron). Optional <strong>Spread publish dates across year</strong> (<code>--spread-year=2026</code>) replaces feed dates, so do not use it for a hand-scheduled calendar or a one-off editorial such as <code>docs/atoms-collections/young-men-unused-to-hard-talk.atom</code>. Internal links are rewritten using <code>base_url</code>. PAGE entries are skipped unless opted in. Existing slugs are skipped unless update is chosen. Needs <code>add_posts</code> (and <code>edit_posts</code> to overwrite).</p>
<p><strong>Schedule &amp; pin:</strong> Status Published plus a future <strong>Publish at</strong> time keeps the post off the public site, RSS, and sitemap until then. <strong>Pin to top</strong> lists it first on the blog and in featured widgets. Admin lists show those as <em>scheduled</em>.</p>
<p><strong>Public reading:</strong> Posts show reading time, related posts, previous/next, an on-page table of contents when there are two or more h2/h3 headings, last-updated when the post was edited more than an hour after publish, author archive links, and tracker-free Share (copy / email / native share). Logged-in editors with <code>edit_posts</code> can preview drafts and scheduled posts with <code>?preview=1</code>.</p>
<p><strong>Archives &amp; search:</strong> Month archives at <code>/blog/archive/YYYY/MM</code>, year archives, author pages at <code>/blog/author/{username}</code>. Site search at <code>/search</code> covers published pages and posts (the Search widget uses that). 404 pages offer the same search.</p>
<p><strong>SEO &amp; social:</strong> SEO title, meta description (150–160 chars), featured share image (1200×630 recommended), optional <code>noindex</code>, and <strong>content width</strong> override (full / wide / normal / narrow) for the public post layout.</p>
<p><strong>LLM / AI:</strong> Plain-language summary for assistants; JSON at <code>/blog/{slug}.json</code>; Schema.org <code>BlogPosting</code> on the public HTML. Listed in <code>/llms.txt</code> when published and not noindex.</p>
<p><strong>Citation / BLUF:</strong> One-sentence citation snippet for AI passage extraction; optional FAQ Q&amp;A pairs for Schema.org <code>FAQPage</code>. Site-wide citation policy: System → General → AI search &amp; citation.</p>
<p><strong>Comments:</strong> Visitors can leave comments when enabled under General → Discussion. Moderate under <code>/admin/comments</code>.</p>
<p><strong>Featured image:</strong> Upload or pick on the post form. Used on the blog listing and as Open Graph / Twitter Card image. Recommended size: <strong>1200×630 px</strong>. Public URL: <code>/share/media/{id}</code>.</p>
<p>Admin: <code>/admin/posts</code></p>
<p><strong>Visual builder demo:</strong> <code>npm run test:e2e:cms-builder-drag-column-size</code> (headed) shows drag reorder, column width 1–12, edge resize, and min height on a published page. Same builder is used for posts via <strong>Edit via Frontend editor</strong>.</p>
<p><strong>While logged in:</strong> Public post pages show <strong>Edit via Frontend editor</strong> and <strong>Edit in admin</strong> for users with <code>edit_posts</code>.</p>
